   814	\section{Experiments}\label{sec:experiments}
   815	%======================================================================
   816	
   817	All experiments were pre-registered: predictions, decision rules, designs and metrics were
   818	committed before any pre-registered run (\texttt{notes/dcltheorem\_prereg.md}, commit
   819	\texttt{05d2bf5}; this was \texttt{3550e24} before a history rewrite, see
   820	\texttt{COMMIT\_SHA\_MAP.md}). The algorithm sees only $N$; the harness samples pairs
   821	uniformly from $\Sn$ and assigns outcome classes after the fact.
   822	
   823	\subsection{Designs and metric}
   824	\begin{itemize}
   825	\item \textbf{C1 (primary)} is the algorithm of Section~\ref{sec:alg} (four bands, $\ell\equiv3\bmod4$,
   826	  base $2$, $n$-only parameters) with a finite-size height schedule: $H$ is the smallest
   827	  value with block-0 multiplicity $\lambda_0=|V|\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal P_0}1/\ell\ge3$, which corresponds
   828	  to $H\asymp\sqrt n$. This lies \emph{below} the range of Corollary~\ref{cor:polylog}, where the
   829	  proved bound $n^2/H^2$ is vacuous. The experiments therefore test correctness, the lemmas
   830	  and the cost exponent, not the proved exceptional rate.
   831	\item \textbf{C2}: C1 with $\lambda_0\ge\ln(P/\ln P)+2$ (heuristic full coverage), $n\le64$.
   832	\item \textbf{C3}: C1 with all odd band primes, Tonelli--Shanks roots and a charged
   833	  least-nonresidue search.
   834	\item \textbf{HH}: a calibrated operational Harvey--Hittmeir implementation, with Bluestein
   835	  chirp powers charged.
   836	\item \textbf{Metric} $E$: $n$-bit modular-multiplication equivalents,
   837	  $E=\mathrm{mul}_N+\mathrm{mul}_{\mathrm{small}}+\mathrm{poly}+\lceil\log_2n\rceil(\mathrm{gcd}_N+\mathrm{inv}_N)
   838	  +\lceil\mathrm{bigmul\ bits}/n\rceil$, with polynomial work charged as
   839	  $\sum(D+1)\lceil\log_2(D+2)\rceil$ (FFT model). $E$ is a proxy; it is not the proof of
   840	  Theorem~\ref{thm:main}(ii). $E_{\mathrm{first}}$ counts the blocks up to the first that yields
   841	  a factor, $E_{\mathrm{full}}$ all four blocks.
   842	\end{itemize}
