   310	whereas all semiprimes number asymptotically \(X\log\log X/\log X\). Thus trial division up to \(N^\delta\) factors a density-one proportion of unrestricted semiprimes in \(N^{\delta+o(1)}\) time. This is an elementary deduction from the counting asymptotics, not a new factoring mechanism. It has only an inverse-\(\log\log X\) relative exceptional estimate and says nothing comparable about balanced semiprimes. [Crişan–Erban, *On the counting function of semiprimes*](https://arxiv.org/html/2006.16491v2).
