   403	### 3.8 Costs outside the search (not solved here)
   404	
   405	- **Order of γ = β^L.** ord_p(γ) = ord_p(β)/gcd(ord_p(β), L). It becomes small when p − 1 is
   406	  divisible by two or more of the moduli, which happens with probability
   407	  ≈ (Σ_{ℓ∈𝒫}1/ℓ)²/2 ≍ (log u/log Y)².
   408	  - Then the baby list repeats mod p. That reveals p by gcd (class PM1) unless it is
   409	    simultaneously small mod q.
   410	  - **The deterministic order lemma for L-th powers is open (UNVERIFIED).**
   411	    Oznovich–Volk give order ≥ D in D^{1/2+o(1)}, but for β, not β^L.
   412	- **Small factors.** Removing factors ≤ N^{1/3} by Pollard–Strassen costs N^{1/6+o(1)}
   413	  (r10). That is at the same exponent, so it is no obstruction to 1/6 but blocks going
   414	  lower.
   415	
   416	### 3.9 Unbalanced range (limitation; heuristic)
   417	
   418	For q/p ≈ R ≫ 1, the weights need B/A ≈ R, and F's span grows to ≈ √(RN).
   419	- With per-band baby lists the band costs ≈ (RN)^{1/6}. With the shared list it costs
   420	  R^{1/4}N^{1/6}.
   421	- Summing over dyadic R up to N^{1/3} gives N^{2/9} or N^{1/4}. That is worse than Harvey,
   422	  whose Lehman pairs ab ≤ r cover all ratios at once.
   423	- So DCL as specified is a balanced-range method. A uniform-ratio version is
   424	  **not yet tested**.
   425	
   426	## 4. The three orchestrator inputs
   427	
   428	- **Gray-code / Stage-3 leaves (user).**
   429	  - Agreed, and it is the content of Thm C. Any all-classes scheme keeps
   430	    #leaves ≍ φ(M)·m₀ = N^{1/5}; only the generation cost changes.
   431	  - DCL reduces the number of **distinct leaves** to N^{1/6+o(1)}.
   432	  - Each DCL leaf covers a whole residue class across the range, P/M ≈ (PW)^{1/2}
   433	    candidates, the maximum allowed by (1). An HH leaf covers about P^{1/3}W^{2/3}·N^{−o(1)}.
   434	- **r10 warnings.**
   435	  - (3) Separate bases: solved by γ = β^L (§2.3). The baby lists coincide as group elements.
   436	  - (4) Base generation: §3.8, open for L-th powers.
   437	  - (2) UW / He–Sahai: §3.6.
   438	- **Chirp / quadratic-in-k leaves (user).** Leaves Y_k = Y₀γ₁^kγ₂^{k²} cost O(1) to
   439	  generate, but Stage 3 is the product tree ∏_k(X − Y_k) evaluated at the baby points. Its
   440	  cost is Õ(#leaves + #babies) however the leaves were made, so cheap generation saves only
   441	  Stage 2.
   442	  - Could chirp leaves cover more exponents per leaf? No. The covered exponent set is
   443	    E = {e_k + j}, with |E| ≤ #leaves·#babies, so the sumset bound |B|·|G| ≥ W is unchanged.
   444	  - Each window W_k is set by the unknown p inside a bucket, (√(ap) − √(bq))², not by
   445	    centre truncation (orchestrator (ii)). So the number of leaves Σ_k⌈W_k/m⌉ is the same as
   446	    without the chirp.
   447	  - When leaves and babies share β, the double product over (leaves × babies) is literally
   448	    the 1-D test over E. The chirp is a Stage-2 constant, as you expected.
   449	  - **Refuted for this model** (as an exponent improvement).
   450	
   451	## 5. Prior art (GPT-6.1-sol check, 2026-10-18; curated)
   452	
   453	- **Ingredients (PROVED as prior art).**
   454	  - Lehman 1974: multipliers.
   455	  - McKee 1999: a modulus-squared restriction "if a prime m divides …", heuristic N^{1/4+ε}.
   456	  - Hittmeir 2018: modular-hyperbola sieving over many small primes.
   457	  - Harvey 2021: a shared collision search over multiplier families, and Alg. 4.1.
   458	  - HH 2022 Prop. 3.3: the class lock, with a single modulus and lattice-chosen weights.
   459	  - Hart 2012: one-line factoring, many multipliers, heuristic N^{1/3}.
   460	- **Not found (UNVERIFIED that none exists).** No source with the union over many prime
   461	  moduli near N^{1/6} with fixed small weights, nor with the cofactor-exponent shared baby
   462	  list. We claim nothing beyond "no prior formulation found by us".
   463	- **Context.** A heuristic N^{1/6} is not a general factoring milestone: ECM and QS are
   464	  conjecturally subexponential. The interest is only within the deterministic
   465	  collision-search line (Harvey/HH/UW).

